+// RiscV64LclByteWise: under strict alignment (JitRiscV64StrictAlign), a scalar
+//   stack access to a local whose frame offset is not a multiple of the access
+//   width is done byte-wise. Stack locals are pointer-aligned, so the offset within
+//   the local (GT_LCL_FLD) plus, for a dependently promoted struct field, the
+//   field's offset within its parent (packed structs) decides. Register candidates
+//   never reach memory here and are excluded.
